WEBVTT

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.630
<i>It wasn't me.</i>

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.700
<i>That's right. Even then...</i>

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.230
<i>I didn't kill him.</i>

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.080
<i>It wasn't my fault!</i>

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.350
<i>That's right.</i>

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.560
<i>Even then...</i>

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.030
You're afraid of the ocean?

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:59.490
I nearly drowned when I was a kid.
The adults thought I was playing...

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:01.200
and just stood on the shore,
watching and laughing.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:03.790
What's a guy like that
doing on this project?

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:07.040
Because this thing will
keep me from drowning.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:12.050
- Go? You are?
- Yeah.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.050
I formally volunteered yesterday.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:18.720
You're talking crazy!

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:24.060
Aren't you interested?
He had money, fame, position.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.770
Why would such an important
scientist start all this?

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.770
Aren't you interested?

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.530
Know what this is?

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.280
A composite?

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.450
It was taken by a recon drone.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.290
That's what's inside the thick clouds
our spy sats can't peek through.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.290
So, wanna check it out?

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:59.260
You scared? We're transmitting
the signal. They won't kill us.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.430
That's assuming Zorndyke's
in the mood to talk to us.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.140
- He is.
- How do you know that?

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.520
<i>Just because.</i>

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.790
Starboard high! Something big!

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.420
- That's!
- The Phantom Ship!

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:36.500
Leave it alone, Hayami!
We have no intention of attacking.

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:58.820
- Katsuma!
- Go on without me, Hayami!

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:03.910
- God dammit! He ignored our signal.
- Never mind. Just go!

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.000
- Almost... Almost got it!
- I'm fine! Just go!

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.300
Just go! Go now!

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:22.050
KATSUMA!

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.890
<i>"See you around, Hayami."</i>

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.480
<i>I didn't kill him.</i>

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:23.150
<i>Smack in the middle of the Pacific.</i>
<i>Helluva one-way ticket.</i>

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.090
You...

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:45.550
You saved me?

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.610
You want me to eat this?

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.610
You sure?
Isn't it a friend of yours?

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:14.620
We're enemies, you know.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:18.620
You want to thank me?

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:53.330
<i>All I do is get rescued.</i>

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.000
<i>By Katsuma.</i>

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.460
<i>And also...</i>

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:11.220
<i>All I do is</i>
<i>get rescued from the sea.</i>

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:28.860
Hey.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:33.240
Are you guys happy about this?

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:37.660
If this pole shift succeeds,
we'll lose our place to live.

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:40.540
And then we'll vanish
from the Earth soon after.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:45.130
Then you guys will
create a new world.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:50.470
A world of endless blue.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:54.220
A utopia covered
by the waters of life.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:57.810
Are you happy about that?

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:06.610
Zorndyke rejects the world as it is.
Does that mean we're unhappy?

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:10.820
Maybe he wants nature to punish us
for all the destruction...

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.070
we cause
by pursuing our ambitions.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:20.710
No, that's not right.
He isn't any sort of ecologist.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:24.580
And I don't think
he went nuts, either.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:29.380
Would he kill a billion people
just for that?

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:31.970
So, why is Zorndyke...?

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:34.430
"Aren't you interested?"

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:02.250
Some good luck mixed in with the bad.
Damage in the engine room's light...

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:04.580
and our hull repairs
should be completed soon.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:08.880
Out of 7 boats, 2 are heavily damaged
and 1 moderately damaged.

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:11.090
That's not what I call good luck.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:15.970
But the operation's begun.
There's no turning back now.

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:32.740
You should rest.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:34.820
I'm fine.

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:40.830
Thinking about him?
You reap what you sow.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:41.910
Stop it.

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:44.660
We're fighting to avenge
a billion people.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:48.250
No, to let mankind keep on living!

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:51.750
There's no room in that fight for
an outsider who acts like a cowboy.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:55.340
- Am I wrong?
- I don't think you're wrong.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:58.510
Then you're going to
have to forget about him!

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:03.020
He left while we were fighting.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:07.650
Even if he survives, we'd leave
a bad taste in each other's mouths.

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:23.370
- We've sighted it!
- Coordinates 22-16-00. Right on target!

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:27.080
Confirmed. We've arrived at the
target point! Picking up beacon!

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:29.460
So, we're finally here.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:33.250
Yeah. Our last card to play.

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.100
- An inheritance from the old days, huh?
- Heh, an inheritance?

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.480
Nasty things to lose,
don't you think?

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:50.560
- They're nuclear-tipped, aren't they?
- SLBMs.

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:54.610
A Typhoon-class sub
rigged as a giant torpedo...

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:59.360
carrying 20 SLBMs rigged
for simultaneous ignition.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:02.030
The flashiest
firecracker in the world.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:06.000
Send out the Grampus.
Begin the operation!

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:09.870
<i>That's right.</i>
<i>There's no turning back now.</i>

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:30.350
"Kill him, kill him," huh? The same...
It's the same thing, all over again.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:46.740
Kill me. If it'll make you happy,
then do it.

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:50.410
A billion people
are already dead.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:54.000
One or two more won't make
much of a difference.

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:12.140
What the...?

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:20.610
This is...

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:22.990
A Musuca-class...?!

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:27.700
<i>You saved her.</i>

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:34.000
<i>You saved Mutio.</i>

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:02.110
What's going on?

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:05.950
<i>The women have</i>
<i>returned to the sea.</i>

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:09.700
<i>Now you must return</i>
<i>to where you belong.</i>

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.160
That doesn't exist anymore.

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:15.210
The place I was born is
on the bottom of the sea now.

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:20.210
<i>Where you belong exists</i>
<i>neither on the land nor in the air.</i>

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:26.300
Are you saying...?

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:30.640
<i>Your companions still live.</i>

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:53.500
- Isn't the work finished yet?
- 30 more minutes, Boss!

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:56.080
I want it done NOW!
Damn it all.

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:59.290
- Um, uh. Boss?
- What is it?

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:04.260
- We're getting a signal from the Mutio.
- You know where the women went?

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:07.050
Well, uh. After Blue Dome
was destroyed...

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:10.050
it seems one of
Blue 6's crew was spared.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:11.260
WHAT?

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:15.390
Why did they save a human?
They're the enemy!

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:16.770
The enemy we have to kill!

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:18.770
Well, yes sir, but...

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:23.940
Damned thieving cats!
They lie. Kill. Steal!

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:26.740
That's what
they're really like!

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:29.780
- Uh, cats, sir...?
- Idiot!

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:34.040
- Onloading completed, Boss!
- You're sure of what we've got?

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:38.830
Aye, sir. 13 cruise missiles,
6 torpedoes, 8 depth charges.

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:40.880
All of them nuclear-armed.

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:45.550
Excellent. We'll burn
the humans to death...

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:47.880
with the unquenchable fire
they created themselves!

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:51.390
What a show this will be.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:55.270
But, Boss. The order to
destroy them hasn't come!

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:56.640
Just SHUT UP!

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:04.780
Papa's methods are too soft!
When it's time to kill, you kill.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:09.990
The humans see their chance, they'll be
advancing into our territory soon.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.660
Kill them! Annihilate them all!

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:17.710
Kill! Kill!
Kill! Kill! Kill!

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:25.460
<i>We were born beneath</i>
<i>the thick ice of the Antarctic.</i>

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:28.340
<i>Inside the culture tanks.</i>

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:33.430
<i>We were to wander the seven seas</i>
<i>and destroy human cities.</i>

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:36.350
<i>That was our purpose.</i>

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:40.140
<i>But, one day, a question</i>
<i>arose among my kind.</i>

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:47.230
<i>Why did Papa</i>
<i>grant us sentience?</i>

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:52.360
How much of the Man-yo-shu
have you learned so far?

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:57.580
" 'Today, today!' Each day
I have waited for you..."

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:01.500
"and now do they not say you are
strewn with the shells of Ishi River?"

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:05.670
I'll be finished with the
Chronicle of Garia soon.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:08.170
Wonderful. Good girl.

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:11.510
Brother Verg is so late.

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:15.550
Yes. Troublesome boy.

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:19.890
I hope nothing bad
will happen to him.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:25.520
<i>Why did he?</i>
<i>Aren't you interested, human?</i>

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:28.900
<i>Because he's testing us?</i>

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:31.860
<i>I am not nearly</i>
<i>so arrogant as that.</i>

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:35.950
<i>Those who walk on the land</i>
<i>and those who swim in the sea.</i>

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:39.870
<i>Two life-forms,</i>
<i>set to kill each other.</i>

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:49.420
<i>He won't be the one</i>
<i>who decides this.</i>

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.800
<i>Will it be us who decide?</i>

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:54.130
<i>Isn't that right, Katsuma?</i>

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:58.970
<i>I'm interested myself, now.</i>
<i>About this man called Zorndyke.</i>

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:07.360
<i>Seabed rise. Range: 2000!</i>

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:10.570
Engines, one-half.
Left rudder, 25 degrees.

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:13.110
This is like trick riding.

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:22.410
<i>Overhead outcropping. Range: 600!</i>
<i>It's not on the charts!</i>

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:28.960
Engines, slow. Left rudder, 8 degrees.
Up trim, 12! No. 14 degrees!

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:33.420
This is nuts!
We'll never make it through!

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:38.430
- Down trim, 15 degrees!
- Aye, aye!

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:59.030
There's no better guide
for us than him.

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:05.910
This is the path he took
to make peace with Zorndyke.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:10.040
Every nook and cranny is
etched into his memory.

00:18:10.670 --> 00:18:12.800
A path to peace, huh?

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:20.050
And now it's being used as our last chance
to destroy him. Ironic, isn't it?

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:25.770
Up trim, 5 degrees!
Left rudder. And return!

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:29.060
It's quiet.

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:35.530
The flagship Coback should be cracking
their rear line with the Atlantic Fleet.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:39.570
- That should keep the enemy nice and busy.
- I hope so.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:43.330
We're behind schedule, but we get
the choice part of this mission.

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:45.580
Too bad for the Atlantic Fleet...

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:49.080
but we'll be the ones
who finish off the enemy.

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:53.710
- Bio-motor contact!
- What?

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:55.920
Verifying sound profile.
It's a Musuca!

00:18:57.380 --> 00:19:02.350
Boss! Musuca 22 is approaching
the Blue Fleet by itself!

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:04.180
What did you say?

00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:08.310
At this rate, they're going
to give our position away!

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:12.690
Number 22? That defective prototype
who wandered away from the herd?

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:15.190
It looks like a human and
a woman are with him.

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:18.900
- Should we help him?
- No, wait.

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:24.410
Let them kill him.
Let the Blue's kill him.

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:29.750
Captain! The Grampus is better
suited for this narrow channel!

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:31.580
Order me out to attack with
some torpedoes!

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:33.460
Wait. It could be a trap.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:36.960
Sonar shows it's alone.
No escorts.

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:38.970
Maybe it's a scout.

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:43.180
- Strange.
- Musuca, closing range!

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:46.970
Sonar! Go to active search!

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:49.230
Opening torpedo tubes!

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:53.270
Message to all ships!
Take formation around the Typhoon!

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:57.230
- Musuca's speed is unchanged.
- Anti bio-ship warheads 1 and 2, loaded!

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:59.740
Range: 5200 and closing.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:03.700
- Torpedo tubes are flooded!
- Active homing range set!

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:06.370
Number 1 and 3 torpedoes
set for speed mode 3!

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:09.250
Musuca has changed course.
Range: 5000.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:13.250
- He's on a collision course!
- A suicide run? Captain!

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:19.760
Number 1 and 3 tubes, fire!
Take out that Musuca!

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:22.510
No, don't!

00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:37.020
Hayami?

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:39.030
That's what Huang says.

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:43.410
Kino!

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:48.160
You're in too close!
If they attack again...

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:52.160
<i>My words do not reach them.</i>

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:54.670
<i>Go now.</i>

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:57.670
Are you telling me...?
You knew this would happen?

00:20:58.420 --> 00:21:05.140
<i>The lifespan of a prototype is brief.</i>
<i>I've swam far enough.</i>

00:21:07.510 --> 00:21:11.520
<i>I've seen the auroras of the north,</i>
<i>the whales of the south.</i>

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:16.690
<i>The migrating birds of the east, and</i>
<i>the playful dolphins of the west.</i>

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:23.900
<i>It is enough.</i>
<i>My life shall end here.</i>

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:28.200
I hear the song.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:30.870
Song?

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:34.710
<i>Colored blue. Piercing.</i>
<i>A sad song.</i>

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:38.170
You really did it, you bastard.

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:46.970
<i>Go now! To where you belong!</i>
<i>You saved Mutio.</i>

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:52.640
<i>I think Papa would like to</i>
<i>meet a man like you.</i>

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:54.640
Hayami!

00:21:58.020 --> 00:21:58.690
Kino?

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:02.820
Ha... ya mi.

00:22:03.150 --> 00:22:05.320
<i>Go! Go now!</i>

00:22:27.300 --> 00:22:27.970
Hayami!

00:22:29.760 --> 00:22:32.760
All I do is get rescued
from the sea.

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:38.900
So, you're piloting it...
You've gotten better.

00:22:40.940 --> 00:22:42.520
Not as good as you.

00:22:51.450 --> 00:22:54.830
Hey... HEY!

00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:05.800
<i>He is calling for you.</i>
<i>Go to him now.</i>

00:23:10.140 --> 00:23:14.220
<i>Thank you.</i>
<i>It doesn't hurt anymore.</i>

00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:19.310
<i>No more cold.</i>
<i>No more loneliness.</i>

00:23:21.860 --> 00:23:24.480
If we don't stop this, it'll be
a slaughter for both sides.

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:29.150
Pawns killing other pawns. No different
from any of the old wars!

00:23:29.280 --> 00:23:32.120
You son of a...! I don't know
what you picked up from the enemy...

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:35.990
but the operation's already started!
We can't stop it now!

00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:40.170
They're a lot smarter
than you think they are!

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:44.170
Mutio's people are starting
to leave for the Antarctic!

00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:47.670
They've seen our attack
coming for a long time!

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:49.010
What?

00:23:49.840 --> 00:23:52.180
Then what are you
saying we should do?

00:23:53.140 --> 00:23:54.180
Zorndyke.

00:23:56.520 --> 00:23:59.680
Meet Zorndyke and find
out what he's really after!

00:23:59.810 --> 00:24:02.730
It's not to late to stop us
from fighting to the death!

00:24:03.690 --> 00:24:06.940
If we don't, this war
will never really be over.

00:24:07.650 --> 00:24:11.820
Land and sea, each side
fighting the other forever.

00:24:11.910 --> 00:24:13.530
That's what Katsuma said!

00:24:14.910 --> 00:24:16.490
And now I understand.

00:24:17.160 --> 00:24:22.040
But this operation is being put
on by every country on Earth.

00:24:22.170 --> 00:24:24.380
Our opinion isn't going
to change anything.

00:24:24.460 --> 00:24:28.260
That's why... That's why
I'm asking YOU to do this.

00:24:29.630 --> 00:24:30.880
Commander Iga.

00:24:32.390 --> 00:24:33.220
Incoming!

00:24:33.890 --> 00:24:38.770
Sonar contacts! Multiple bio-motors
closing! It's the Phantom Ship!

00:24:39.640 --> 00:24:44.270
You see that, people?
They killed our comrade, AKAHAGE!

00:24:45.060 --> 00:24:50.570
Kill them all! Burn away
all traces of the humans!

00:24:55.530 --> 00:25:00.250
None of this talk matters.
Both sides demand blood...

00:25:00.370 --> 00:25:04.670
and the only paths left are
life or death. One or the other.

00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:09.500
Message to all ships!
Ahead full, combat speed!

00:25:09.590 --> 00:25:11.090
Break out of the
enemies encircling us!

00:25:11.170 --> 00:25:14.090
Ahead full on main
and auxiliary drives!

00:25:14.930 --> 00:25:18.390
Defend the nukes, even if
it takes every ship we have!

00:25:18.560 --> 00:25:21.350
This is it!
We fight to the death!

00:25:39.750 --> 00:25:44.310
<i>Ne ikenai anata ni fureta
Tell me, is it wrong? I want to touch you.</i>

00:25:44.310 --> 00:25:47.200
<i>Kasanaru yori fukai
Deeper and deeper into you.</i>

00:25:47.200 --> 00:25:49.090
<i>Sweet whisper...</i>

00:25:49.090 --> 00:25:53.710
<i>Modokashi ore
I want to vanish...</i>

00:25:53.710 --> 00:25:56.890
<i>Takata ni kieta
...into the foam in the tantalizing orange light...</i>

00:25:56.890 --> 00:26:00.460
<i>Tsuki e no michi wo
Will the moonlight path on the waves...</i>

00:26:00.460 --> 00:26:05.510
<i>Anata e to tsuzuku kashira
...lead me to you, I wonder...</i>

00:26:05.510 --> 00:26:10.020
<i>Wasurerarenai atsui manazashi
I can't forget that warm gaze...</i>

00:26:10.020 --> 00:26:14.500
<i>Soshite amai toiki
...and that sweet sigh.</i>

00:26:18.890 --> 00:26:22.530
<i>Susarei de lullaby
That whispered lullaby...</i>

00:26:27.900 --> 00:26:31.910
<i>Eien lullaby
That eternal lullaby...</i>

00:26:32.440 --> 00:26:36.800
<i>Come whisper to me and touch me...</i>

00:26:36.800 --> 00:26:41.280
<i>Tokimeki wa ren'ai kotoba wa ren'ai
I'm dizzy from my beating heart, don't need any words now.</i>

00:26:41.280 --> 00:26:44.470
<i>Whisper love...</i>

00:27:01.420 --> 00:27:10.270
<i>Setsunaku ayamii anata no toiki ni
Your dangerous sigh that almost breaks my heart...</i>

00:27:10.700 --> 00:27:13.460
<i>Just whisper...</i>

00:27:14.020 --> 00:27:17.930
<i>...and love sweet touch.</i>

00:27:28.250 --> 00:27:37.230
<i>Setsunaku ayamii anata no toiki ni
Your dangerous sigh that almost breaks my heart...</i>

00:27:37.230 --> 00:27:41.270
<i>Sweet whisper... dakaredai
Sweet whisper... I want to embrace you...</i>

00:27:41.270 --> 00:27:43.520
<i>...and love sweet touch.</i>

00:27:43.950 --> 00:27:46.010
<i>Mitaretai
I want to go mad...</i>

00:27:46.180 --> 00:27:55.030
<i>Setsunaku ayamii anata no toiki ni
Your dangerous sigh that almost breaks my heart...</i>

00:27:55.370 --> 00:27:59.090
<i>Sweet whisper... Mitaretai
Sweet whisper... I want to go mad...</i>

00:27:59.090 --> 00:28:01.870
<i>...and love sweet touch.</i>

00:28:01.870 --> 00:28:04.170
<i>Kutsuretai
I want to crumble away...</i>

00:28:04.170 --> 00:28:08.590
<i>Agareru omoe wa
These burning feelings...</i>

00:28:08.590 --> 00:28:13.040
<i>Mina soko ni nemure
...are sleeping deep inside of everyone.</i>

00:28:13.570 --> 00:28:18.310
<i>Yume tsumeru made
Until we awaken from this dream...</i>

00:28:18.790 --> 00:28:20.710
<i>Sweet whisper...</i>

00:28:21.730 --> 00:28:29.130
<i>Mina soko ni nemure...
Sleeping deep inside everyone...</i>

00:28:46.470 --> 00:28:50.680
<i>Blue Submarine No. 6.</i>
<i>Final episode: "Minasoko."</i>
